<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Endecott</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1601–1665</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as John Endicott</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Endecott was an English Puritan who led the advance party of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massachusetts-bay-company">Massachusetts Bay Company</a> to Salem in 1628. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-winthrop">John Winthrop</a>'s arrival he remained a leading magistrate and served as governor of the Massachusetts Bay Colony for more years than anyone else, including most of the 1650s, and was known for his harsh treatment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quakers">Quakers</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-endecott.jpg" alt="John Endecott" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjamin Blyth · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gov._John_Endecott.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
